# SYNOPSIS

```usage
vx dtc in.dts [-o out.dtb] [-I dir ...] [--cc clang] [--check]
```

# DESCRIPTION

`vx dtc` compiles the devicetree source <in.dts> into <out.dtb>, a flattened tree (version 17) such as the loader reads.
The source goes through the C preprocessor first, the toolchain's clang (or <--cc>), as the kernel's sources have it: `#include` and `#define` run, with the source's directory and each <-I> directory searched for headers.

It reads `/dts-v1/` sources: nodes and properties with labels, overrides of a labelled node (`&label { ... };`) or of a path (`&{/soc} { ... };`), `/delete-node/`, `/delete-property/`, `/omit-if-no-ref/` and `/include/`.
A value is a string, a list of cells (`<...>`) whose cells are numbers, character literals, C expressions in parentheses or references, a list of cells of another size (`/bits/ 8`, `16` or `64`), a byte string (`[00 11 22]`), or a reference to a node, which becomes that node's path; values join with commas.
A reference in cells becomes the phandle of the node it names: a node given one by its source keeps it, and the rest are numbered from 1, past those, in the order they are first referred to.
A node marked `/omit-if-no-ref/` that nothing refers to is left out.

The boards' trees are built this way into the ESP's `dtb/`, from upstream's sources in `firmware/dts/`.

<--check> also judges the tree as devmgr would take it, as a whole machine's description, and exits 1 if it finds anything; <-o> is then optional.
It reads the drivers' records under `drivers/`, so it runs from the repository's root.
The checks, each of which prints a line a finding, `check: subject: what`:

: `overlap`
  Two devices' register ranges overlap, and neither lies wholly inside the other.
: `unowned`
  An enabled device that no `driver` record matches and no `leave` record covers (driver(6)); one both cover; one that two drivers match alike.
: `providers`
  A link (a clock, reset, supply, GPIO or the rest) that has no provider or names a device that isn't there, or providers that make a cycle.
  A fixed clock the tree lists ends a chain.
: `iommu-supply`
  A master that is in a power domain, behind an IOMMU unit that has no supply of its own; or behind a unit no device holds and no `leave` record names.
: `interrupts`
  An interrupt that two devices a driver is bound to have.
: `stream-ids`
  A stream id that two masters have on one IOMMU unit.
: `pages`
  A 4 KiB page of registers that two hosts are granted: each device a driver is bound to is a host, granted what devmgr grants it.

# EXAMPLES

```text
% cd firmware/dts
% vx dtc riscv/spacemit/k1-orangepi-rv2.dts -I include -o /tmp/rv2.dtb
% cd ..
% vx dtc --check -I firmware/dts/include \
    firmware/dts/vectraos/spacemit/k1-orangepi-rv2.dts
```

