# DIAGNOSTICS

A source error names its file and line, those of the source before preprocessing: `dtc: soc.dtsi:12: no node labelled 'uart9'`, `expected ';'`, a value that doesn't fit its cells, and it exits 1; `dtc: the preprocessor failed on <file>`.
<--check> prints a line for each finding and `<file>: N devices, M findings`, and exits 1 if there are any.

# BUGS

`/memreserve/` and `/plugin/` (overlays) are refused.
Labels on values and properties are read and dropped, and the tree has no `__symbols__`.
<--check> reads only a devicetree machine's tree; a machine whose firmware gives ACPI is checked from its captured tables by the board tests (`vx test --host BoardCheckTests`), which skip when the capture (`vx acpi import`) is absent.
The registers' offsets are not checked against a spec's tables.
